\section{The dependency contract}

The allowed edges between concepts. A concept may only reference chunks from
concepts it is permitted to depend on. Anything not listed is FORBIDDEN and
fails the conformance gate. If nothing is forbidden, no architectural decision
has been made.

@c --- machine-readable; edit these to match your concepts ---
% ARCH-ALLOW: <concept-b> -> <concept-a>
% ARCH-ALLOW: <concept-c> -> <concept-b>
% ARCH-ALLOW: <concept-c> -> <concept-a>

<In prose, say what is deliberately NOT allowed and why — e.g. "the domain
must not depend on its API surface; lower layers must not depend on higher
ones." Make the forbidden edges explicit so a reader understands the shape.>
